WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:42.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:43.106 --> 00:50.071
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:50.155 --> 00:51.573
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND INCIDENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

4
00:51.656 --> 00:53.074
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED UNDER GUIDELINES

5
00:54.909 --> 00:56.744
EPISODE 13

6
00:56.828 --> 00:57.662
What…

7
00:59.205 --> 01:00.498
did you just do?

8
01:02.917 --> 01:04.169
Did you send a bomb

9
01:05.962 --> 01:07.755
to the residence through the pneumatic tube?

10
01:11.259 --> 01:12.719
Answer the question. Did you?

11
01:17.265 --> 01:19.893
Is that why Hanako…

12
01:23.646 --> 01:24.522
Answer me.

13
01:32.947 --> 01:33.948
I'm sorry.

14
01:36.451 --> 01:37.994
I'm so sorry.

15
01:48.504 --> 01:49.339
Put the gun down.

16
01:55.261 --> 01:56.971
She knew nothing about it.

17
01:57.764 --> 01:59.515
She only made the call as I told her.

18
02:04.604 --> 02:05.772
I'm sorry

19
02:06.606 --> 02:07.523
about your sister.

20
02:11.402 --> 02:12.737
But your father

21
02:13.780 --> 02:14.989
deserves to die.

22
02:22.288 --> 02:23.289
Mr. Sato!

23
02:24.582 --> 02:27.502
Those two Josenjings are in on it together.

24
02:29.254 --> 02:30.672
I heard everything.

25
02:32.715 --> 02:35.843
They were plotting the whole thing.

26
02:37.303 --> 02:39.180
Keum Seo-hee is a spy!

27
03:12.630 --> 03:13.548
Hanako.

28
03:15.883 --> 03:16.759
Hanako.

29
03:18.553 --> 03:19.387
Hanako!

30
03:19.470 --> 03:22.181
Hanako!

31
03:23.474 --> 03:24.309
Hanako!

32
03:24.392 --> 03:26.561
-Hanako! -Hanako!

33
03:27.270 --> 03:29.355
Hanako, open your eyes.

34
03:29.439 --> 03:30.356
Hanako!

35
03:39.782 --> 03:40.783
Hanako.

36
03:47.915 --> 03:48.916
It's the study!

37
03:49.500 --> 03:51.002
Protect the inspector general!

38
03:51.961 --> 03:54.964
Go to His Excellency's residence and get him to safety.

39
03:55.048 --> 03:57.425
A bomb might've been sent from the Government-General.

40
03:57.508 --> 03:58.509
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir!

41
03:59.802 --> 04:00.636
Philip.

42
04:01.804 --> 04:02.638
Philip!

43
04:03.431 --> 04:05.266
Philip!

44
04:05.808 --> 04:07.310
Philip!

45
04:07.393 --> 04:08.478
Philip.

46
04:24.660 --> 04:26.579
You can't find Keum Seo-hee?

47
04:28.664 --> 04:29.582
We have an emergency.

48
04:29.665 --> 04:30.958
We have an emergency.

49
04:31.042 --> 04:32.335
A subversive has sent explosives

50
04:32.418 --> 04:35.588
from the pneumatic tube room to the inspector general's residence.

51
04:35.671 --> 04:37.548
We have an emergency.

52
04:39.759 --> 04:42.053
All guards, report to the pneumatic tube room immediately!

53
04:42.136 --> 04:44.722
All personnel, remain at your posts!

54
04:44.806 --> 04:45.640
I repeat!

55
04:45.723 --> 04:47.767
Report to the pneumatic tube room immediately!

56
04:47.850 --> 04:49.519
We have an emergency.

57
04:49.602 --> 04:51.437
See?

58
04:51.521 --> 04:53.147
They're the ones--

59
05:08.246 --> 05:11.249
We'll say Mitarai was a spy who gave outsiders access

60
05:11.874 --> 05:12.917
to the Government-General.

61
05:16.087 --> 05:17.630
Let's get Ms. Lee out of here first.

62
05:18.589 --> 05:19.966
Seems we're on the same page.

63
05:23.177 --> 05:24.137
Mr. Sato.

64
05:24.887 --> 05:25.972
Not now. Later.

65
05:27.265 --> 05:29.350
Let's get out of here. Then we can talk.

66
05:37.817 --> 05:38.651
Drop the gun.

67
05:40.027 --> 05:41.195
Wait, just a second.

68
05:41.279 --> 05:42.113
Drop the gun!

69
05:50.246 --> 05:53.291
Use me as a hostage, and you can get out of here.

70
05:53.374 --> 05:54.625
Don't give me that bullshit.

71
05:55.626 --> 05:59.172
You expect me to believe you, a lapdog of the Japanese?

72
06:00.339 --> 06:03.342
I just shot a Government-General official,

73
06:04.427 --> 06:06.137
and my little sister is dead.

74
06:07.096 --> 06:09.640
And yet here I am, because I want to save you two.

75
06:09.724 --> 06:10.892
What more can I do

76
06:11.893 --> 06:13.478
to prove myself?

77
06:14.061 --> 06:15.354
Do you think I'd fall for that?

78
06:17.648 --> 06:19.817
Bring your father here. He might still be alive.

79
06:22.278 --> 06:23.488
Let her go.

80
06:23.571 --> 06:25.990
I'll kill you in front of your father.

81
06:26.491 --> 06:27.325
You'll pay

82
06:28.409 --> 06:31.370
for what you did to my brother.

83
06:32.455 --> 06:33.915
What are you talking about?

84
06:34.499 --> 06:35.666
Did you forget already?

85
06:36.626 --> 06:37.960
You killed him

86
06:38.711 --> 06:41.214
right here in the Government-General at the banquet!

87
06:58.564 --> 07:00.191
The cook…

88
07:02.235 --> 07:03.402
He was your brother?

89
07:03.986 --> 07:06.447
That's right. He was my brother.

90
07:13.788 --> 07:14.664
Police!

91
07:14.747 --> 07:16.332
Drop your weapons and surrender!

92
07:22.713 --> 07:24.799
I'm Sato Hideo from the Foreign Affairs Division.

93
07:25.841 --> 07:27.885
I'm in here. Don't do anything yet!

94
07:27.969 --> 07:30.096
The inspector general's son?

95
07:30.763 --> 07:32.640
Mr. Sato, are you okay?

96
07:34.892 --> 07:36.227
Yes, I'm fine.

97
07:36.310 --> 07:37.478
That's a relief.

98
07:37.562 --> 07:39.981
No one was hurt at the inspector general's residence!

99
07:41.857 --> 07:42.692
No one

100
07:43.442 --> 07:44.443
was hurt?

101
07:50.449 --> 07:51.409
So…

102
07:54.245 --> 07:56.330
Is my little sister safe too?

103
07:57.582 --> 07:58.958
Your little sister?

104
08:01.460 --> 08:04.005
Yes. She's safe, as far as we know.

105
08:14.974 --> 08:15.975
I see.

106
08:17.351 --> 08:18.686
Please wait a moment!

107
08:18.769 --> 08:19.604
Yes, sir!

108
08:26.569 --> 08:27.486
I did not

109
08:28.696 --> 08:29.697
kill your brother.

110
08:29.780 --> 08:30.740
Don't lie to me.

111
08:33.159 --> 08:34.118
We don't have time.

112
08:35.161 --> 08:37.788
Get Ms. Lee out first, making it look like she's your hostage.

113
08:37.872 --> 08:39.749
Then take me hostage so you can get out.

114
08:40.291 --> 08:42.460
They can't shoot me. I'm the inspector general's son.

115
08:42.543 --> 08:43.377
No.

116
08:44.545 --> 08:45.671
I'll let her go.

117
08:46.839 --> 08:48.466
But I'm not leaving here.

118
08:49.425 --> 08:50.635
Bring your father to me.

119
08:51.802 --> 08:53.888
I'll make him watch me kill you.

120
08:53.971 --> 08:57.308
Then I'll kill him and myself

121
08:58.601 --> 08:59.518
with this bomb.

122
09:05.900 --> 09:07.068
That means you lose.

123
09:07.943 --> 09:08.778
What?

124
09:08.861 --> 09:10.196
Once my father gets here,

125
09:11.280 --> 09:13.741
the police will storm into this room.

126
09:13.824 --> 09:14.742
Then you'll die.

127
09:16.202 --> 09:18.496
My father wouldn't care if I died.

128
09:19.288 --> 09:22.375
He'd use my death for Japanese propaganda against the independence fighters.

129
09:22.458 --> 09:24.251
Did you forget I have a bomb?

130
09:24.335 --> 09:26.212
If you set that bomb off,

131
09:27.963 --> 09:30.716
only you will die, and my father will be safe.

132
09:32.343 --> 09:33.427
Your brother's death…

133
09:35.429 --> 09:36.263
will be in vain.

134
09:39.016 --> 09:41.936
But if you take me hostage,

135
09:42.478 --> 09:44.021
you can make it out alive.

136
09:44.105 --> 09:45.815
They would never shoot me.

137
09:45.898 --> 09:49.318
I never intended to leave here alive in the first place!

138
09:54.240 --> 09:55.324
Still…

139
09:59.495 --> 10:02.540
you have comrades waiting for you out there.

140
10:05.459 --> 10:08.295
They must be desperately wishing for you to come out alive.

141
10:10.464 --> 10:11.966
Just as you desperately wished

142
10:13.175 --> 10:14.427
for your brother…

143
10:16.804 --> 10:18.556
to return safely.

144
10:25.271 --> 10:26.105
I…

145
10:27.732 --> 10:29.233
did not kill your brother.

146
10:31.402 --> 10:34.989
I have no intention of killing you, and I don't want you to die.

147
10:35.072 --> 10:36.824
If you still want me dead,

148
10:37.491 --> 10:39.702
make it out alive today

149
10:40.369 --> 10:42.163
and wait for another chance to kill me.

150
10:47.626 --> 10:48.544
As long as you live…

151
10:51.630 --> 10:52.965
you'll get another chance.

152
10:56.719 --> 10:57.636
Se-hwan.

153
10:58.220 --> 11:01.640
If something happens to me tomorrow--

154
11:01.724 --> 11:02.767
Come on.

155
11:02.850 --> 11:05.269
Don't say that. That's bad luck.

156
11:06.937 --> 11:10.024
That's why I said if.

157
11:13.944 --> 11:14.779
Even so,

158
11:15.404 --> 11:19.200
you have to live to see Joseon become independent.

159
11:23.537 --> 11:26.499
You can't die before you see Joseon gain independence.

160
11:28.292 --> 11:31.420
Remember how I fought to save you during the Great Kantō Disaster.

161
11:33.923 --> 11:34.840
Stay alive.

162
11:36.175 --> 11:37.009
Se-hwan.

163
11:39.053 --> 11:40.179
As long as you live,

164
11:41.680 --> 11:43.015
you'll get another chance.

165
11:58.823 --> 12:00.324
Interpreter Sato is in there?

166
12:00.407 --> 12:02.493
Yes, it seems he's being held hostage.

167
12:03.911 --> 12:04.912
Break down the door.

168
12:06.580 --> 12:09.750
Then Interpreter Sato could get hurt.

169
12:09.834 --> 12:12.545
I don't care! Break down the door and arrest them all!

170
12:19.009 --> 12:20.469
Keum Seo-hee!

171
12:20.553 --> 12:21.470
Mr. Sato!

172
12:26.350 --> 12:27.685
Back off, all of you!

173
12:28.519 --> 12:30.855
If any of you try anything,

174
12:31.480 --> 12:33.941
I'll kill the inspector general's son!

175
12:37.278 --> 12:39.613
What should we do, Chief?

176
12:41.532 --> 12:42.366
Back off!

177
12:46.412 --> 12:47.705
The woman goes first.

178
12:57.464 --> 12:58.674
She has nothing to do with it.

179
13:08.809 --> 13:10.603
She has nothing to do with it!

180
13:17.443 --> 13:18.277
Lee Ga-kyung.

181
13:20.946 --> 13:22.698
Can you trust me just this once?

182
13:25.242 --> 13:28.787
No matter what I do or say?

183
13:35.544 --> 13:36.420
Yes.

184
13:38.339 --> 13:39.173
I trust you.

185
13:45.763 --> 13:46.847
Don't die.

186
13:47.973 --> 13:48.891
Please.

187
13:53.938 --> 13:55.814
Now walk. Nice and slow.

188
14:01.362 --> 14:03.405
Don't even think about pulling anything,

189
14:03.489 --> 14:04.782
or I'll shoot you.

190
14:06.408 --> 14:07.409
All right.

191
14:09.495 --> 14:11.455
Everyone, please move back.

192
14:14.333 --> 14:15.417
Back off, all of you!

193
14:26.136 --> 14:27.221
What's going on?

194
14:30.933 --> 14:32.351
Se-hwan.

195
14:36.814 --> 14:37.648
Stand back!

196
14:39.817 --> 14:40.818
Stand back!

197
14:46.782 --> 14:47.783
Stand back!

198
15:02.006 --> 15:04.425
Make sure Keum Seo-hee stays safe.

199
15:05.759 --> 15:06.677
No need to tell me.

200
15:07.928 --> 15:09.304
I was going to do that anyway.

201
15:10.180 --> 15:11.015
You must be

202
15:11.974 --> 15:13.142
in love with her.

203
15:15.144 --> 15:18.731
I took you for a clever Japanese lapdog, but you've fallen for a spy.

204
15:20.149 --> 15:21.608
I wish your father knew about it.

205
15:28.240 --> 15:29.658
You'd better stay alive too.

206
15:30.701 --> 15:31.660
See you again soon.

207
15:33.203 --> 15:34.121
All right.

208
16:52.908 --> 16:54.451
Get the inspector general to safety!

209
16:54.535 --> 16:55.369
Sir!

210
16:55.452 --> 16:56.703
It's dangerous. This way!

211
17:23.355 --> 17:24.189
Se-hwan.

212
17:25.399 --> 17:26.567
Go after them!

213
17:36.994 --> 17:38.162
Hold on tight.

214
17:51.758 --> 17:52.676
What the hell?

215
17:56.597 --> 17:57.723
Move the car!

216
17:57.806 --> 17:59.016
Get the car out of here!

217
17:59.099 --> 18:00.225
Turn the car around!

218
18:01.143 --> 18:02.269
Hey, you!

219
18:02.352 --> 18:03.478
What the hell are you doing?

220
18:03.562 --> 18:05.814
Sorry, that car came out of nowhere--

221
18:07.441 --> 18:08.275
I'm sorry.

222
18:13.780 --> 18:15.616
I've seen that guy somewhere before.

223
18:15.699 --> 18:16.658
I'm so sorry.

224
18:26.168 --> 18:28.462
Mr. Sato, please move over there.

225
18:37.095 --> 18:38.263
He's still alive!

226
18:47.648 --> 18:48.482
Songjeon.

227
18:49.858 --> 18:50.943
Are you watching over me?

228
18:54.112 --> 18:55.155
Guess what?

229
18:56.365 --> 18:58.325
I got a job at Gyeongdo Noodle House.

230
19:40.993 --> 19:42.077
The Gugukdan?

231
19:45.414 --> 19:48.083
First the opening ceremony,

232
19:48.166 --> 19:49.793
and now they planted a spy

233
19:49.876 --> 19:52.838
as the pneumatic tube system's on-site supervisor

234
19:53.672 --> 19:55.799
and sent a bomb to the residence?

235
19:56.550 --> 19:58.176
They've been making a mockery

236
19:58.260 --> 20:00.387
of the Government-General under our noses.

237
20:01.096 --> 20:03.765
What the hell have you been doing all this time?

238
20:03.849 --> 20:05.058
Your Excellency.

239
20:05.142 --> 20:06.018
At that time, I--

240
20:06.101 --> 20:08.312
Is the Government-General's security

241
20:08.395 --> 20:11.148
no better than a shop door in the marketplace?

242
20:12.607 --> 20:14.568
Please forgive me, Your Excellency!

243
20:15.152 --> 20:17.362
The League of Nations Commission of Enquiry

244
20:17.446 --> 20:19.239
is coming soon.

245
20:19.823 --> 20:22.409
Instead of showing them a peaceful Joseon,

246
20:22.492 --> 20:24.661
are you planning to show complete chaos,

247
20:24.745 --> 20:26.830
with bombs going off everywhere?

248
20:26.913 --> 20:27.748
Sato!

249
20:28.582 --> 20:33.337
You said you knew how to handle them because you were born in Joseon.

250
20:33.420 --> 20:37.341
Look at you, letting those Josenjings make a fool of you.

251
20:37.424 --> 20:39.343
Is this what you meant by handling them?

252
20:40.844 --> 20:42.596
I'm sorry, Your Excellency!

253
20:44.514 --> 20:47.309
I made all the preparations to round them all up,

254
20:48.268 --> 20:50.437
but the officers on the ground misjudged the situation.

255
20:50.520 --> 20:52.147
"Misjudged the situation"?

256
20:53.398 --> 20:55.525
You've let the Gugukdan make a fool of you.

257
20:55.609 --> 20:58.528
You couldn't even get the Gyodang-ri slums under control.

258
20:58.612 --> 21:01.323
Is there anything you can do right?

259
21:02.491 --> 21:04.368
You're not getting away with this.

260
21:05.035 --> 21:07.329
The Japanese government is keeping an eye on this.

261
21:09.247 --> 21:10.665
Because of this mess,

262
21:10.749 --> 21:13.502
I'm being summoned to Tokyo.

263
21:13.585 --> 21:14.628
Your Excellency.

264
21:15.337 --> 21:16.880
Before you leave,

265
21:16.963 --> 21:18.548
I'll make sure we deliver

266
21:18.632 --> 21:21.635
concrete results on both the Gugukdan and Gyodang-ri.

267
21:22.260 --> 21:23.178
Results?

268
21:25.138 --> 21:28.850
You've already shown me plenty of results.

269
21:30.143 --> 21:34.022
I'll decide what to do with you when I get back.

270
21:34.106 --> 21:35.190
Until then,

271
21:36.149 --> 21:37.401
keep your heads down.

272
21:41.530 --> 21:43.490
Yes, Your Excellency.

273
21:44.991 --> 21:46.368
Yes, Your Excellency!

274
21:53.333 --> 21:56.420
After everything I went through to get where I am,

275
21:57.129 --> 22:00.132
he thinks he can cast me aside over those worthless fools?

276
22:00.674 --> 22:01.800
Like hell he will!

277
22:04.845 --> 22:05.720
Inspector General.

278
22:05.804 --> 22:09.182
I clearly ordered to arrest Keum Seo-hee just as you instructed.

279
22:09.266 --> 22:11.935
But my incompetent subordinates botched the operation.

280
22:12.602 --> 22:13.645
I assure you, though,

281
22:13.728 --> 22:16.106
I'll make sure Gyodang-ri is dealt with.

282
22:16.189 --> 22:17.232
I'll send the police now--

283
22:17.315 --> 22:19.192
"Send the police"?

284
22:20.652 --> 22:22.237
You imbecile!

285
22:26.658 --> 22:29.870
Do you want a shootout before the Commission arrives in Joseon?

286
22:29.953 --> 22:32.622
I gave that troublesome land to Kim Seung-eok for a reason.

287
22:32.706 --> 22:33.874
Do I have to spell it out?

288
22:35.208 --> 22:37.461
You get someone else to do your dirty work.

289
22:37.544 --> 22:41.882
Imagine the fallout if things go wrong and the foreign press catches wind of it.

290
22:41.965 --> 22:44.509
Did you learn nothing from Kyeam-ri?

291
23:00.650 --> 23:03.028
The one who told us to shoot them in Kyeam-ri

292
23:04.196 --> 23:05.363
was you.

293
23:13.788 --> 23:15.999
So you were born in Shanghai?

294
23:16.082 --> 23:18.710
Give me your parents' names and address.

295
23:19.419 --> 23:21.588
My husband's been taken to the hospital.

296
23:21.671 --> 23:23.048
I'll answer when he gets here.

297
23:23.131 --> 23:25.217
Just answer the question.

298
23:25.300 --> 23:26.927
Are you really Chinese?

299
23:32.432 --> 23:33.350
Inspector General!

300
23:58.792 --> 24:05.215
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

301
24:18.478 --> 24:21.898
Inspector General, I believe there's been some misunderstanding.

302
24:21.982 --> 24:23.441
-Why is Mrs. Yoo-- -Misunderstanding?

303
24:27.779 --> 24:28.822
Keum Seo-hee.

304
24:30.407 --> 24:31.241
Yes?

305
24:31.324 --> 24:34.286
Why did you give her your dead daughter's name?

306
24:36.079 --> 24:38.290
Did you need a replacement for your dead kid?

307
24:45.964 --> 24:47.173
You should resent her.

308
24:50.510 --> 24:53.054
It's her fault for giving you the name Keum Seo-hee.

309
24:57.684 --> 24:58.518
Got nothing to say?

310
25:01.229 --> 25:03.982
Will you keep your mouth shut like your husband did

311
25:05.650 --> 25:06.901
even if I shoot her dead?

312
25:13.283 --> 25:16.703
You just don't care if she dies because she's not your real daughter?

313
25:20.373 --> 25:22.667
Well, let's find out.

314
25:23.752 --> 25:24.753
Wait!

315
25:31.092 --> 25:34.012
If what you just said was true…

316
25:38.224 --> 25:40.310
then shooting me dead right here

317
25:41.436 --> 25:43.146
would be pointless, wouldn't it?

318
25:46.441 --> 25:48.360
They wouldn't speak even when their own child died.

319
25:48.943 --> 25:51.571
Why would they care about me dying

320
25:52.280 --> 25:53.698
just because I share her name?

321
25:55.158 --> 25:56.159
You're quite the talker.

322
25:58.828 --> 25:59.746
Mrs. Yoo

323
26:00.455 --> 26:01.915
doesn't speak Japanese very well.

324
26:06.670 --> 26:10.215
I'm not sure what happened between you two.

325
26:11.049 --> 26:12.092
But, Inspector General,

326
26:12.801 --> 26:15.303
if you want to know about them,

327
26:15.845 --> 26:17.597
wouldn't it be better

328
26:18.682 --> 26:19.516
to use me

329
26:20.517 --> 26:22.894
than to kill me?

330
26:36.199 --> 26:38.910
Joseon women really do have a reckless streak.

331
26:40.078 --> 26:41.663
It can get them killed

332
26:42.163 --> 26:43.081
or keep them alive.

333
26:52.549 --> 26:53.508
Keum Seok-jung

334
26:54.884 --> 26:56.344
died in that very spot.

335
27:03.560 --> 27:05.145
No, sir! You can't go in!

336
27:05.228 --> 27:06.062
You can't!

337
27:06.771 --> 27:07.731
Get out of my way!

338
27:16.489 --> 27:17.449
Honey.

339
27:19.993 --> 27:21.661
Sir, can you explain this?

340
27:21.745 --> 27:22.996
Why'd you arrest my wife?

341
27:23.705 --> 27:26.624
She knew a bomb would arrive through the pneumatic tube.

342
27:26.708 --> 27:29.586
Don't you recall the bombing at the pneumatic tube opening ceremony?

343
27:31.129 --> 27:34.132
Every paper received disturbing tips blaming the independence fighters,

344
27:34.215 --> 27:35.800
so I warned her to stay alert.

345
27:35.884 --> 27:38.136
That's why my wife thought it might be a bomb

346
27:38.219 --> 27:40.096
and rushed to save your daughter.

347
27:40.180 --> 27:41.931
How is that a crime?

348
27:43.683 --> 27:44.726
Well, Inspector General?

349
27:44.809 --> 27:47.520
Have I ever put the Government-General in a difficult position?

350
27:48.980 --> 27:52.525
Regardless of what other foreign journalists say about Joseon,

351
27:52.609 --> 27:55.528
I've always been fair and truthful in my coverage.

352
27:55.612 --> 27:57.405
Even after the bombing at the banquet,

353
27:57.489 --> 28:00.533
I was the only one who reported the Government-General's position!

354
28:07.081 --> 28:08.875
Out of respect for you,

355
28:08.958 --> 28:12.962
I even asked the head of our Far East branch who's coming to Gyeongseong

356
28:13.046 --> 28:16.758
with the League of Nations Commission, to meet you privately for tea.

357
28:16.841 --> 28:19.260
After all that, how can you treat me like this?

358
28:21.095 --> 28:22.555
My wife is American too.

359
28:24.390 --> 28:27.435
Does Japan usually lock up foreigners without any evidence?

360
28:27.519 --> 28:28.895
Then you'll have to arrest me too.

361
28:31.940 --> 28:33.399
My wife rushed to the study

362
28:33.483 --> 28:35.735
because I'd told her to watch out for a bomb.

363
28:45.078 --> 28:47.121
You're a journalist through and through.

364
28:47.914 --> 28:50.917
That was very logical and convincing, almost as if you'd rehearsed it.

365
28:53.920 --> 28:55.129
Just as you told me.

366
29:00.760 --> 29:01.970
Escort them home.

367
29:02.679 --> 29:03.513
Yes, sir!

368
29:06.683 --> 29:08.601
Guard their home until further notice.

369
29:08.685 --> 29:11.145
Don't let a single soul get in or out.

370
29:11.229 --> 29:13.106
Yes, sir!

371
29:13.189 --> 29:14.357
Just as you said,

372
29:15.024 --> 29:16.526
given how disturbing things are.

373
29:19.112 --> 29:20.113
Shall we go, honey?

374
29:26.411 --> 29:28.246
Keum Seo-hee, you're staying here.

375
29:33.835 --> 29:35.461
We should finish our conversation.

376
29:47.181 --> 29:49.726
What did you want to talk about?

377
29:52.228 --> 29:54.188
Are you planning to use me?

378
29:57.191 --> 29:58.109
Or…

379
30:00.528 --> 30:02.155
are you going to kill me?

380
30:02.238 --> 30:03.156
Neither.

381
30:05.033 --> 30:06.242
It won't be me who kills you.

382
30:07.076 --> 30:08.536
It'll be them.

383
30:11.122 --> 30:13.833
Now that you've been alone with me,

384
30:15.710 --> 30:17.462
they will never trust you again.

385
30:19.923 --> 30:21.174
Go ask them…

386
30:23.635 --> 30:25.803
about my dead Joseon wife.

387
30:27.847 --> 30:28.681
She was a spy

388
30:30.058 --> 30:32.518
the Gugukdan sent to me.

389
30:36.356 --> 30:37.357
What did you say?

390
30:41.694 --> 30:43.363
So they did keep it from you.

391
30:44.948 --> 30:47.617
They sent someone as young as you to work as a spy.

392
30:48.660 --> 30:50.495
They really are ruthless.

393
30:54.207 --> 30:55.249
A spy?

394
30:59.253 --> 31:00.129
You mean me?

395
31:01.339 --> 31:03.049
No, I'm not a spy.

396
31:03.716 --> 31:06.844
You know that. I used to be their live-in maid.

397
31:06.928 --> 31:09.722
Now I'm an English interpreter trainee at the Government-General.

398
31:09.806 --> 31:10.723
If you say so.

399
31:12.934 --> 31:14.727
They did make sure you looked the part.

400
31:17.480 --> 31:19.107
No matter how loyal you are,

401
31:20.149 --> 31:22.694
the Gugukdan will kill you once you're no longer useful.

402
31:24.946 --> 31:26.280
That's how she died too.

403
31:28.574 --> 31:29.867
It belongs to my mother.

404
31:29.951 --> 31:31.786
I'm looking for my mother,

405
31:32.829 --> 31:34.706
but I don't even know her name yet.

406
31:36.290 --> 31:39.252
You may tell Hideo the truth, if that's what you want.

407
31:39.335 --> 31:41.963
It seems like you and my son have become quite close.

408
31:43.214 --> 31:44.424
I'll let you decide.

409
31:56.102 --> 31:57.895
You stink.

410
32:00.106 --> 32:01.190
It's the smell of someone

411
32:01.274 --> 32:05.278
who crawled their way out of the muck just to survive.

412
32:10.742 --> 32:12.827
You're just like me.

413
32:34.682 --> 32:35.808
You have the same eyes.

414
32:42.023 --> 32:44.442
Do you think killing me will bring Joseon's independence?

415
32:45.443 --> 32:46.277
No.

416
32:47.070 --> 32:48.488
It will never happen.

417
32:49.989 --> 32:51.491
And yet those Gugukdan bastards

418
32:51.574 --> 32:54.285
keep manipulating innocent people and dragging them to their graves,

419
32:54.368 --> 32:55.578
just as they've done to you.

420
32:57.205 --> 32:59.207
Even if you die here and now,

421
32:59.290 --> 33:01.209
they won't lift a finger to keep you alive

422
33:01.834 --> 33:04.462
or even try to save you.

423
33:06.422 --> 33:08.091
So many people have died already,

424
33:08.174 --> 33:11.052
but they won't stop this lunacy. Don't you get it?

425
33:21.395 --> 33:22.230
You have five days.

426
33:24.649 --> 33:27.944
Bring me proof that Yoo Philip and his wife are with the Gugukdan.

427
33:29.612 --> 33:30.571
Proof that his wife

428
33:31.447 --> 33:33.491
was Keum Seok-jung's wife will also suffice.

429
33:35.993 --> 33:37.870
Do that, and I'll spare your life.

430
33:37.954 --> 33:40.206
But if you can't…

431
33:43.709 --> 33:45.253
it'd be a shame to waste your talent,

432
33:45.336 --> 33:46.838
but I'll kill you first.

433
33:48.631 --> 33:50.133
Just like Keum Seok-jung,

434
33:50.716 --> 33:51.884
who died right here.

435
33:54.679 --> 33:56.347
Don't even think about running.

436
33:59.851 --> 34:00.893
Because…

437
34:05.648 --> 34:08.442
I can track you down and kill you at any time.

438
36:12.775 --> 36:14.819
I don't care if you're a spy or not.

439
36:16.988 --> 36:18.406
Just promise me.

440
36:21.826 --> 36:23.619
Promise me you won't die.

441
36:29.333 --> 36:30.167
Please.

442
36:33.379 --> 36:35.089
Please, just stay alive,

443
36:36.007 --> 36:36.841
Ga-kyung.

444
36:39.927 --> 36:41.554
You promise me too.

445
36:43.472 --> 36:44.432
Promise

446
36:45.308 --> 36:46.767
you won't die.

447
37:56.754 --> 37:57.838
What are you doing?

448
37:57.922 --> 38:01.133
Sato will want hard evidence linking us to the Gugukdan.

449
38:01.217 --> 38:03.302
I'm sure he told her to bring that proof.

450
38:04.387 --> 38:07.848
Philip, Seo-hee gave up going to America and came back for us.

451
38:07.932 --> 38:09.558
Unlike before, I trust her too.

452
38:09.642 --> 38:11.352
But we're dealing with Ishikawa.

453
38:11.435 --> 38:14.605
Ishikawa was known for his ruthless and devious interrogations

454
38:14.688 --> 38:16.899
at Jongno Police Station.

455
38:17.983 --> 38:19.860
So we have to take precautions.

456
38:20.569 --> 38:22.446
And this doesn't just put us at risk.

457
38:22.530 --> 38:24.907
It could put the entire Gugukdan in danger.

458
38:24.990 --> 38:27.159
She knows so much about us, after all.

459
38:35.042 --> 38:35.876
So-ran.

460
38:38.421 --> 38:39.338
Don't forget.

461
38:40.923 --> 38:43.676
She's not your daughter, Seo-hee. She's Lee Ga-kyung, the pickpocket.

462
38:43.759 --> 38:44.593
That girl

463
38:46.387 --> 38:48.431
is only Seo-hee because you called her that.

464
38:54.311 --> 38:58.315
Does she have anything that could prove we're members of the Gugukdan?

465
39:00.943 --> 39:01.777
Yes.

466
39:03.195 --> 39:05.281
The identity guarantee letter for her trip to America

467
39:06.157 --> 39:08.367
and the Government-General staff booklet Suzuki made.

468
39:08.451 --> 39:09.326
I have one condition.

469
39:10.161 --> 39:11.370
I need you to promise me

470
39:12.663 --> 39:15.583
that when Seo-hee comes back, you'll hear her out first

471
39:16.792 --> 39:18.252
instead of doubting or accusing her.

472
40:08.886 --> 40:10.471
I found the identity guarantee letter.

473
40:13.265 --> 40:14.266
I found the booklet.

474
40:19.396 --> 40:20.814
What do you think you're doing?

475
40:23.943 --> 40:25.027
I asked what you're doing.

476
40:35.454 --> 40:36.288
What's this for?

477
40:39.166 --> 40:40.876
Did you go through my things

478
40:42.169 --> 40:43.587
to take these back?

479
40:44.630 --> 40:45.464
Why?

480
40:46.173 --> 40:47.216
Calm down.

481
40:47.299 --> 40:49.051
I'll explain everything, so just calm down.

482
40:49.635 --> 40:50.761
You want me to calm down?

483
40:51.679 --> 40:52.846
I just

484
40:53.722 --> 40:56.141
risked my life to carry out the operation.

485
40:56.225 --> 40:57.142
After all that,

486
40:58.769 --> 41:00.437
this is what you're doing to me?

487
41:01.564 --> 41:03.857
We just needed to make sure.

488
41:03.941 --> 41:05.484
Make sure of what?

489
41:06.068 --> 41:07.444
What did you and Sato talk about?

490
41:12.157 --> 41:12.992
What?

491
41:16.745 --> 41:19.790
You think I might have tipped him off.

492
41:19.873 --> 41:21.709
That's why you're doing this?

493
41:22.334 --> 41:25.629
Do you think I'll bring these pieces of paper to Sato?

494
41:25.713 --> 41:27.006
I want an answer.

495
41:28.340 --> 41:30.050
How did you escape the Government-General,

496
41:30.134 --> 41:32.219
and what did you and Sato discuss at Jongno Station?

497
41:32.845 --> 41:33.721
Mr. Yoo.

498
41:33.804 --> 41:34.638
Seo-hee.

499
41:35.848 --> 41:37.516
Just tell us what happened.

500
41:37.600 --> 41:39.310
If nothing happened, just say so--

501
41:39.393 --> 41:41.562
Is it that hard for you to trust me?

502
41:44.106 --> 41:45.274
Do you…

503
41:47.359 --> 41:49.695
Do you have any idea how terrified I was today?

504
41:52.781 --> 41:55.159
Even if he was an awful Japanese man,

505
41:55.242 --> 41:58.037
I saw someone die right in front of me.

506
41:58.954 --> 42:00.748
And that naengmyeon deliveryman…

507
42:04.960 --> 42:06.962
Your comrade Se-hwan.

508
42:08.005 --> 42:10.674
I did my best to find a way to make it out alive with him.

509
42:10.758 --> 42:11.675
But…

510
42:17.097 --> 42:17.931
I made it out

511
42:19.183 --> 42:20.434
by making it look like

512
42:20.517 --> 42:23.020
he'd been holding me hostage.

513
42:23.729 --> 42:26.732
Interpreter Sato offered himself as a hostage to get him out,

514
42:26.815 --> 42:28.108
but it didn't work out.

515
42:28.192 --> 42:30.944
After that, I was taken to Jongno Police Station.

516
42:31.028 --> 42:32.571
That's all there is to it.

517
42:35.366 --> 42:39.703
Interpreter Kim Tae-ung shot that Japanese man to save us.

518
42:42.706 --> 42:43.540
Wait.

519
42:45.459 --> 42:46.418
Kim Tae-ung?

520
42:50.255 --> 42:51.715
You mean Sato Hideo?

521
42:53.467 --> 42:54.301
Yes.

522
42:56.720 --> 42:58.305
That's his Joseon name.

523
43:02.226 --> 43:06.563
I told you never to develop feelings for Sato Hideo, didn't I?

524
43:07.690 --> 43:10.943
That's how you stay alive as a spy.

525
43:16.949 --> 43:17.866
Well, actually…

526
43:22.746 --> 43:23.664
you said

527
43:25.165 --> 43:27.418
he shot the cook on the day of the banquet.

528
43:30.587 --> 43:32.423
Are you sure you saw it yourself?

529
43:34.591 --> 43:36.176
Could you have been mistaken?

530
43:38.637 --> 43:41.265
You're hoping So-ran was mistaken, aren't you?

531
43:57.656 --> 43:59.450
Thank you so much

532
44:00.117 --> 44:01.160
for saving me.

533
44:05.372 --> 44:06.582
The one who saved you

534
44:08.083 --> 44:09.460
was my wife.

535
44:10.753 --> 44:12.921
Thank you, ma'am.

536
44:13.922 --> 44:15.382
Are you all right?

537
44:15.466 --> 44:16.508
Yes.

538
44:16.592 --> 44:18.385
Are you all right too, ma'am?

539
44:20.345 --> 44:22.890
I've been hoping to meet you someday.

540
44:24.516 --> 44:25.726
Sorry?

541
44:25.809 --> 44:28.103
We already met earlier.

542
44:32.274 --> 44:33.609
Hanako, it's time to go.

543
44:33.692 --> 44:35.527
We should let them get some rest.

544
44:36.069 --> 44:36.904
Okay.

545
44:56.465 --> 44:57.382
Well then.

546
44:57.466 --> 44:59.468
Bye, Hanako.

547
45:00.427 --> 45:01.261
Wait.

548
45:01.345 --> 45:05.098
You sound like the woman on the phone who said she was Hideo's girlfriend.

549
45:06.016 --> 45:06.850
Hanako.

550
45:06.934 --> 45:10.145
Ms. Yanagi's been waiting outside. Let's get going.

551
45:10.229 --> 45:11.104
Yeah.

552
45:11.188 --> 45:12.397
It was her voice.

553
45:13.190 --> 45:14.233
Am I wrong?

554
45:19.404 --> 45:22.115
I'm sorry I didn't listen to you earlier.

555
45:24.368 --> 45:26.161
I'm glad you weren't hurt.

556
45:26.245 --> 45:29.122
See? It was the same voice.

557
45:32.251 --> 45:34.086
We'll be going then.

558
45:34.753 --> 45:36.338
Once again, I'm deeply grateful

559
45:37.798 --> 45:39.174
for saving Hanako.

560
45:41.134 --> 45:42.845
Take care, Mr. Hideo.

561
45:51.687 --> 45:52.521
Bye.

562
46:15.043 --> 46:17.838
I don't think you can do any more work as a spy.

563
46:19.089 --> 46:20.173
I'll find somewhere safe.

564
46:20.257 --> 46:22.134
Quit the Government-General and lie low.

565
46:24.636 --> 46:25.929
No matter how loyal you are,

566
46:26.555 --> 46:28.849
the Gugukdan will kill you once you're no longer useful.

567
46:30.642 --> 46:32.603
No, I'll go to work.

568
46:34.354 --> 46:35.188
What?

569
46:36.315 --> 46:37.816
If I disappear now,

570
46:37.900 --> 46:39.776
it'll look like I'm a spy.

571
46:39.860 --> 46:41.570
-Don't you think? -But…

572
46:43.447 --> 46:44.281
Good night.

573
47:16.271 --> 47:17.105
What?

574
47:19.691 --> 47:20.859
The inspector general

575
47:20.943 --> 47:23.737
ordered you to arrest Sato Hideo?

576
47:23.820 --> 47:24.738
Yes.

577
47:24.821 --> 47:27.532
So we were waiting at Myeongwolgwan for further orders.

578
47:27.616 --> 47:28.700
Myeongwolgwan?

579
47:30.243 --> 47:33.914
Kim Seung-eok's daughter was supposed to meet him at Hwawol.

580
47:33.997 --> 47:37.334
We were told Mr. Sato would come to Myeongwolgwan alone.

581
47:39.169 --> 47:41.088
-Okay. That'll be all. -Yes, sir.

582
47:45.258 --> 47:50.097
It seems he and his beloved son aren't getting along anymore.

583
47:50.180 --> 47:54.226
He can't even keep his own Josenjing son under control,

584
47:55.811 --> 47:59.064
yet he dared to lecture me about Kyeam-ri?

585
48:11.034 --> 48:12.369
I'm sorry, miss.

586
48:16.206 --> 48:19.668
I drove straight at their car without asking you.

587
48:19.751 --> 48:23.005
Now that they've found the gun, it may not be easy to get out.

588
48:25.549 --> 48:26.383
But

589
48:27.050 --> 48:28.844
they'll let you go for sure.

590
48:31.179 --> 48:33.306
I can tough it out here,

591
48:33.932 --> 48:34.850
so don't worry.

592
48:37.811 --> 48:40.856
I'll tell my dad that going to the Government-General was my idea.

593
48:54.870 --> 48:55.912
My apologies.

594
49:02.169 --> 49:03.754
There's been a misunderstanding.

595
49:13.055 --> 49:14.890
Tail those two, and don't let them catch on.

596
49:14.973 --> 49:15.807
Yes, sir.

597
49:19.269 --> 49:20.520
He went that way.

598
49:20.604 --> 49:21.897
He ran out that way.

599
49:21.980 --> 49:24.816
It's a tall, young guy with a mask on.

600
49:26.443 --> 49:28.028
Close the curtains!

601
49:28.111 --> 49:31.073
She's the daughter of the president of Joil Textile Factory.

602
49:33.408 --> 49:36.536
His son is suspicious enough, and now the daughter-in-law too?

603
49:39.581 --> 49:42.084
After being played by that spy bitch,

604
49:42.167 --> 49:43.919
he still hasn't learned his lesson.

605
49:46.546 --> 49:49.466
And he's got the nerve to throw me under the bus?

606
49:55.597 --> 49:58.183
As Interpreter Sato testified, the pneumatic tube room supervisor

607
49:58.266 --> 50:01.728
used a naengmyeon delivery as an excuse to let the Gugukdan into the building.

608
50:02.229 --> 50:04.481
The guard at the side entrance also confirmed it.

609
50:06.233 --> 50:08.819
The follow-up investigation into Interpreter Sato resumes--

610
50:08.902 --> 50:10.195
"Follow-up investigation"?

611
50:11.571 --> 50:12.572
Yes, sir.

612
50:12.656 --> 50:14.783
My son killed the spy

613
50:14.866 --> 50:17.244
and nearly lost his own life as a hostage.

614
50:18.328 --> 50:20.205
What more is there to investigate?

615
50:21.039 --> 50:22.207
The thing is--

616
50:22.290 --> 50:23.416
Are you saying

617
50:23.500 --> 50:25.460
you suspect my own son?

618
50:26.878 --> 50:28.547
Absolutely not, sir!

619
50:28.630 --> 50:30.549
-You're dismissed. -Yes, sir!

620
50:44.688 --> 50:47.274
You can sleep here, just for tonight.

621
50:48.066 --> 50:49.234
Okay.

622
50:49.317 --> 50:51.194
By the way,

623
50:52.445 --> 50:55.532
what do you call "big sister" in the Joseon language?

624
50:55.615 --> 50:57.200
What? Big sister?

625
51:00.245 --> 51:01.204
Unni.

626
51:02.581 --> 51:03.832
"Unni"?

627
51:05.584 --> 51:06.543
Unni.

628
51:07.627 --> 51:09.504
You know what?

629
51:09.588 --> 51:10.797
Yanagi…

630
51:10.881 --> 51:12.507
I mean, Ms. Yanagi said

631
51:12.591 --> 51:16.720
you were going to marry a Joseon woman.

632
51:16.803 --> 51:18.430
Is that "unni" the one?

633
51:20.390 --> 51:21.766
I approve!

634
51:21.850 --> 51:24.102
I like that "unni."

635
51:26.104 --> 51:28.398
I can't believe what that little mouth says.

636
51:29.649 --> 51:30.609
Now go to sleep.

637
51:59.346 --> 52:00.180
How's Hanako?

638
52:01.056 --> 52:01.973
She's asleep.

639
52:02.724 --> 52:03.558
All right.

640
52:04.935 --> 52:06.978
She must've been shaken.

641
52:07.062 --> 52:07.896
Yes.

642
52:10.232 --> 52:11.942
Father will probably lose his position.

643
52:13.485 --> 52:15.111
After what happened at the banquet,

644
52:15.779 --> 52:17.280
today's incident makes it inevitable.

645
52:18.823 --> 52:20.116
If he's forced out,

646
52:21.076 --> 52:22.994
he'll probably never make it back into politics.

647
52:26.957 --> 52:28.541
It's for the best for everyone.

648
52:30.377 --> 52:32.045
It should've happened long ago.

649
52:33.672 --> 52:36.383
What are you going to do?

650
52:38.051 --> 52:39.177
Are you going

651
52:40.345 --> 52:41.513
with your father?

652
52:42.597 --> 52:43.473
To Japan?

653
52:48.687 --> 52:50.438
The inspector general is home.

654
53:55.920 --> 53:57.881
I've told the police everything.

655
53:57.964 --> 53:59.674
I have nothing more to say.

656
54:00.675 --> 54:01.718
Hope you get some rest.

657
54:02.635 --> 54:04.596
Surely you have something to say to me.

658
54:14.397 --> 54:16.191
Being taken hostage was a mistake.

659
54:17.400 --> 54:18.234
I'm sorry.

660
54:20.528 --> 54:22.614
Still, you saved my life, Father.

661
54:22.697 --> 54:26.618
Did you want to save that Josenjing?

662
54:30.622 --> 54:33.500
When you faced that cook who attacked me at the opening ceremony,

663
54:34.167 --> 54:35.335
you hesitated.

664
54:37.212 --> 54:39.923
If I'd left him to you instead of shooting him myself,

665
54:40.465 --> 54:42.717
would you have let yourself be taken hostage then?

666
54:44.844 --> 54:46.012
To save him?

667
54:54.270 --> 54:55.271
Hideo.

668
54:55.980 --> 54:58.233
What's making you so confused?

669
55:06.825 --> 55:08.284
The police told me something.

670
55:10.787 --> 55:12.288
That it wasn't Kim Seung-eok

671
55:12.872 --> 55:14.999
waiting for me today, but his daughter.

672
55:16.668 --> 55:18.545
She was at Hwawol, not Myeongwolgwan.

673
55:20.839 --> 55:23.174
Why did you tell me to go to Myeongwolgwan?

674
55:24.759 --> 55:26.761
Who was waiting for me there?

675
55:28.471 --> 55:29.305
Confused?

676
55:30.473 --> 55:32.016
Aren't you the one who's confused?

677
55:32.100 --> 55:33.309
Shut your mouth, Hideo.

678
55:33.393 --> 55:36.354
It's true I wanted to know what drove those in the Gugukdan.

679
55:36.438 --> 55:37.814
You want to know why?

680
55:37.897 --> 55:39.232
Independence for Korea!

681
55:39.315 --> 55:40.150
Hideo!

682
55:40.233 --> 55:41.860
Because they keep risking their lives,

683
55:41.943 --> 55:45.196
shouting "Independence for Korea" even when they know they'll die.

684
55:45.697 --> 55:47.240
That's why I wanted to know

685
55:47.907 --> 55:50.034
what could possibly drive them to do it.

686
55:51.870 --> 55:55.623
I wanted to know what it was about Joseon's independence

687
55:57.125 --> 55:59.711
that made them risk their lives without the slightest fear.

688
56:01.087 --> 56:02.172
But then…

689
56:07.051 --> 56:08.052
today,

690
56:09.012 --> 56:10.680
they tried to kill Hanako.

691
56:12.849 --> 56:14.517
My one and only sister.

692
56:18.730 --> 56:21.065
I can never forgive them, Father.

693
56:24.319 --> 56:25.695
Instead of doubting me,

694
56:27.113 --> 56:28.198
keep me by your side.

695
56:31.493 --> 56:33.286
I will not betray you.

696
56:36.039 --> 56:37.248
At least, not anymore.

697
57:11.658 --> 57:14.911
Simply because I'm a colonial resident, born and raised in Joseon,

698
57:15.578 --> 57:18.540
I've spent my whole life having to prove myself.

699
57:19.832 --> 57:21.417
This time will be no different.

700
57:21.918 --> 57:23.628
I'll prove myself again.

701
57:24.254 --> 57:26.631
After all I've been through to get this far,

702
57:27.715 --> 57:29.676
I can't go down like this.

703
57:33.054 --> 57:34.347
Have they made you step down?

704
57:37.725 --> 57:39.686
I want you to interpret the farewell speech

705
57:39.769 --> 57:43.439
at Gyeongseong Station on the day the League of Nations Commission leaves.

706
57:44.065 --> 57:46.276
The Government-General's top priority now

707
57:46.359 --> 57:48.152
is the success of the Commission's visit.

708
57:48.820 --> 57:50.280
We must prove

709
57:50.989 --> 57:53.783
that Japan's rule over Joseon is legitimate.

710
57:55.702 --> 57:56.619
That said…

711
57:58.705 --> 58:02.875
though you're Joseon by blood, you're loyal to the Empire of Japan.

712
58:04.127 --> 58:07.046
What better symbol of peace and harmony in Joseon…

713
58:09.173 --> 58:11.009
could there be than you?

714
58:12.343 --> 58:13.428
Would that…

715
58:15.722 --> 58:16.806
help you too?

716
58:16.889 --> 58:17.890
Help?

717
58:20.226 --> 58:21.060
Yes.

718
58:22.979 --> 58:24.272
It most certainly would.

719
58:27.859 --> 58:30.320
Do you think I'll give up so easily?

720
58:32.989 --> 58:33.823
No.

721
58:35.533 --> 58:37.619
I will never back down.

722
58:39.746 --> 58:40.622
Not ever.

723
58:45.668 --> 58:48.087
SIN TAE-JIN

724
59:12.028 --> 59:13.237
You need to leave Gyeongseong.

725
59:22.997 --> 59:24.165
My father already knows

726
59:24.874 --> 59:27.543
who Yoo Philip, his wife, and you really are.

727
59:31.464 --> 59:33.549
I don't mean to disregard your wishes.

728
59:36.803 --> 59:37.637
But…

729
59:37.720 --> 59:38.680
No.

730
59:42.225 --> 59:45.228
It's more dangerous to run at this point.

731
59:47.605 --> 59:51.442
They say it's safest right under the tiger's nose.

732
01:00:10.086 --> 01:00:12.004
Here, take this.

733
01:00:18.136 --> 01:00:19.762
Remember what I told you before?

734
01:00:22.014 --> 01:00:24.183
This pawn ticket belonged to my mother.

735
01:00:27.562 --> 01:00:29.439
Right after she gave birth to Hanako,

736
01:00:30.606 --> 01:00:31.607
she left us.

737
01:00:33.776 --> 01:00:36.279
That's why people assumed she'd died giving birth.

738
01:00:39.949 --> 01:00:40.908
But my father

739
01:00:42.160 --> 01:00:44.871
never said otherwise.

740
01:00:48.124 --> 01:00:49.584
I suppose he was too hurt

741
01:00:50.668 --> 01:00:52.336
by the fact that she'd left him.

742
01:00:58.593 --> 01:00:59.677
I would find myself…

743
01:01:03.264 --> 01:01:04.474
thinking of my mother…

744
01:01:06.559 --> 01:01:08.144
every so often.

745
01:01:10.563 --> 01:01:12.356
Maybe I missed her.

746
01:01:14.942 --> 01:01:15.777
No.

747
01:01:17.612 --> 01:01:19.989
I do miss her.

748
01:01:24.494 --> 01:01:26.412
I don't know why she had a pawn ticket

749
01:01:26.496 --> 01:01:28.706
that belonged to someone named Sin Tae-jin.

750
01:01:30.958 --> 01:01:32.752
But if I find that Jongno Pawnshop

751
01:01:34.170 --> 01:01:36.464
and retrieve the item…

752
01:01:38.883 --> 01:01:41.552
maybe it'll lead me to her.

753
01:01:45.264 --> 01:01:46.682
Mr. Sato.

754
01:01:51.854 --> 01:01:54.482
Though I haven't had any luck yet.

755
01:01:58.236 --> 01:01:59.278
On the day of the banquet,

756
01:02:00.029 --> 01:02:01.322
you returned this to me.

757
01:02:02.406 --> 01:02:03.699
You were leaving, weren't you?

758
01:02:06.869 --> 01:02:08.120
You don't need to answer.

759
01:02:09.413 --> 01:02:10.623
But this time…

760
01:02:13.167 --> 01:02:15.378
you said you wouldn't leave.

761
01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:22.593
So please, keep this with you.

762
01:02:25.972 --> 01:02:27.390
That way, I can feel…

763
01:02:33.479 --> 01:02:35.648
you're safe by my side.

764
01:02:39.694 --> 01:02:40.570
You are…

765
01:02:43.990 --> 01:02:44.991
my vault.

766
01:02:48.077 --> 01:02:50.037
Hold on to it, and next time…

767
01:02:52.498 --> 01:02:53.666
we'll find…

768
01:02:56.460 --> 01:02:58.671
Jongno Pawnshop together.

769
01:04:03.152 --> 01:04:04.820
No matter how loyal you are,

770
01:04:04.904 --> 01:04:07.657
the Gugukdan will kill you once you're no longer useful.

771
01:04:07.740 --> 01:04:09.200
That's how she died too.

772
01:04:14.705 --> 01:04:16.332
Can I keep

773
01:04:17.792 --> 01:04:20.294
trusting you, madam?

774
01:04:28.928 --> 01:04:30.012
Can I keep

775
01:04:31.764 --> 01:04:33.557
trusting you?

776
01:05:08.050 --> 01:05:10.052
Once I walk out of this house,

777
01:05:10.136 --> 01:05:11.929
I might never be able to come back.

778
01:05:14.306 --> 01:05:16.475
Because the Gugukdan could get rid of me.

779
01:05:17.059 --> 01:05:20.271
Once you leave, the police might storm into the house.

780
01:05:23.733 --> 01:05:25.735
Because you could turn us in.

781
01:06:01.145 --> 01:06:02.146
Good morning.

782
01:06:02.730 --> 01:06:04.398
Interpreter Trainee Keum Seo-hee.

783
01:06:10.237 --> 01:06:11.072
Yes?

784
01:06:11.739 --> 01:06:13.282
INTERPRETER TRAINEE KEUM SEO-HEE

785
01:06:15.951 --> 01:06:18.329
Why are my things here?

786
01:06:22.500 --> 01:06:23.417
Good morning, sir.

787
01:06:27.088 --> 01:06:27.963
You're here?

788
01:06:29.048 --> 01:06:31.050
Yamada suddenly decided to quit.

789
01:06:32.843 --> 01:06:34.053
Welcome.

790
01:06:35.096 --> 01:06:36.847
You're my secretary starting today.

791
01:06:41.227 --> 01:06:42.561
Four days left now.

792
01:06:56.575 --> 01:06:57.576
Mr. Suzuki?

793
01:06:59.995 --> 01:07:00.913
Good to see you again.

794
01:07:01.831 --> 01:07:03.958
I was called back to work rather suddenly.

795
01:07:04.041 --> 01:07:05.543
INTERPRETER SUZUKI HIROYUKI

796
01:07:22.893 --> 01:07:23.727
Good morning.

797
01:07:24.353 --> 01:07:25.187
Secretary?

798
01:07:25.813 --> 01:07:26.689
Mr. Sato.

799
01:07:27.523 --> 01:07:28.524
What in the world…

800
01:07:29.108 --> 01:07:32.319
Gyodang-ri is hardly the issue right now, isn't it?

801
01:07:33.445 --> 01:07:35.156
I want to call off the engagement.

802
01:07:35.239 --> 01:07:37.199
Had I known you'd lose your position,

803
01:07:37.283 --> 01:07:40.035
I'd never have signed a marriage contract to begin with.

804
01:07:40.119 --> 01:07:42.246
-"Marriage contract." -If His Excellency finds out--

805
01:07:42.329 --> 01:07:43.289
Mr. Kim.

806
01:07:52.339 --> 01:07:53.507
Keep your voice down.

807
01:07:54.425 --> 01:07:56.719
Are you trying to tell the whole city about our deal?

808
01:07:58.137 --> 01:07:59.555
I mean, first the banquet bombing,

809
01:08:00.222 --> 01:08:02.391
then even your residence yesterday…

810
01:08:02.474 --> 01:08:05.269
The independence fighters have made a complete fool of you.

811
01:08:05.352 --> 01:08:08.981
The Government-General is in shambles. How could you escape the fallout?

812
01:08:09.064 --> 01:08:10.816
So now you want to back out?

813
01:08:10.900 --> 01:08:11.817
Of course.

814
01:08:11.901 --> 01:08:14.195
What kind of businessman would agree to lose money?

815
01:08:14.278 --> 01:08:17.698
Since things have gone south, we should settle up and part ways.

816
01:08:18.824 --> 01:08:20.367
Let's call off the engagement.

817
01:08:21.911 --> 01:08:22.870
Call it off, is it?

818
01:08:23.662 --> 01:08:24.496
Very well.

819
01:08:25.581 --> 01:08:26.957
Then let's settle up first,

820
01:08:27.041 --> 01:08:28.792
just as you suggested.

821
01:08:30.169 --> 01:08:32.087
Do you have the money for the penalty?

822
01:08:32.713 --> 01:08:33.631
Inspector General.

823
01:08:33.714 --> 01:08:36.217
You had no complaints when you got that land cheap.

824
01:08:37.176 --> 01:08:39.929
You were busy counting all the money you'd make off me.

825
01:08:40.012 --> 01:08:41.847
Now you want to ignore the contract?

826
01:08:41.931 --> 01:08:42.765
What?

827
01:08:43.807 --> 01:08:46.727
Let's get our facts straight.

828
01:08:47.561 --> 01:08:49.980
You think I bought that dump because I wanted to?

829
01:08:50.064 --> 01:08:53.400
I only agreed to take on the headache of developing that land

830
01:08:53.484 --> 01:08:57.029
because you promised to back me as inspector general.

831
01:08:57.112 --> 01:09:00.699
But now you're about to lose that position, aren't you?

832
01:09:05.204 --> 01:09:06.580
Who said I'd lose my position?

833
01:09:11.669 --> 01:09:12.628
You have four days.

834
01:09:14.046 --> 01:09:17.258
Clear that miserable Gyodang-ri slum once and for all within four days.

835
01:09:17.341 --> 01:09:19.134
I mean,

836
01:09:19.218 --> 01:09:23.138
you said we had until the Commission arrived to demolish the shantytown.

837
01:09:23.222 --> 01:09:24.056
No.

838
01:09:25.557 --> 01:09:26.433
Four days.

839
01:09:27.559 --> 01:09:28.852
Clear it out completely.

840
01:09:28.936 --> 01:09:31.105
But four days is pushing it.

841
01:09:31.730 --> 01:09:33.857
Those residents are refusing to move.

842
01:09:34.483 --> 01:09:36.777
What if someone ends up dead in the process?

843
01:09:39.822 --> 01:09:41.740
Don't test my patience any further.

844
01:09:42.908 --> 01:09:43.993
Mr. Kim.

845
01:09:57.172 --> 01:09:59.800
So this is a petition to stop the demolition,

846
01:09:59.883 --> 01:10:01.385
and you just need our thumbprints?

847
01:10:01.468 --> 01:10:04.763
That's right. I had it drawn up at a scrivener's office in Jongno.

848
01:10:04.847 --> 01:10:08.851
If Joil Textile, the Government-General, the Keijo Municipal Office, and the press

849
01:10:08.934 --> 01:10:10.519
all see this, they'll have to listen.

850
01:10:11.312 --> 01:10:13.314
It's all pointless.

851
01:10:14.106 --> 01:10:16.900
If that had worked, would we have had to leave home and end up here?

852
01:10:17.776 --> 01:10:20.654
These pieces of paper will end up as toilet paper.

853
01:10:21.572 --> 01:10:24.241
It's better than doing nothing and getting kicked out.

854
01:10:24.325 --> 01:10:25.367
Listen, kid.

855
01:10:25.451 --> 01:10:27.911
I screamed for independence until my throat gave out.

856
01:10:27.995 --> 01:10:31.040
But all I've got is this crippled leg.

857
01:10:31.749 --> 01:10:33.250
They'll kick us out, so don't bother.

858
01:10:33.334 --> 01:10:34.877
Hey, Bak-chun.

859
01:10:34.960 --> 01:10:38.714
Don't you think it's worth giving this petition a shot?

860
01:10:38.797 --> 01:10:40.007
Good grief.

861
01:10:40.090 --> 01:10:41.884
With the money to write the petition,

862
01:10:41.967 --> 01:10:44.345
we might as well buy Kkot-nim a bowl of noodles.

863
01:10:44.428 --> 01:10:45.512
Noodles?

864
01:10:47.806 --> 01:10:48.640
I'm signing.

865
01:10:51.435 --> 01:10:52.603
THE PEOPLE OF GYODANG-RI

866
01:10:54.355 --> 01:10:55.189
Geum-ok.

867
01:10:55.272 --> 01:10:57.024
Why are we always being forced out?

868
01:10:57.524 --> 01:10:58.692
We've lost our country.

869
01:10:58.776 --> 01:11:00.903
If we're thrown out of here, where else can we go?

870
01:11:01.904 --> 01:11:03.989
Are we supposed to take their beatings, obey them,

871
01:11:04.073 --> 01:11:05.824
and leave whenever they tell us to?

872
01:11:05.908 --> 01:11:07.701
No, we're human beings too.

873
01:11:14.458 --> 01:11:16.377
I'll leave on my terms, even if it kills me.

874
01:11:17.252 --> 01:11:18.670
I'm standing my ground here.

875
01:11:20.130 --> 01:11:21.382
I'm tired of being thrown out.

876
01:11:23.884 --> 01:11:25.177
My goodness.

877
01:11:25.677 --> 01:11:27.638
I'm sick of being kicked out too. Give it here.

878
01:11:28.680 --> 01:11:31.600
It's just a thumbprint. I can do it a hundred times over.

879
01:11:31.683 --> 01:11:32.726
Here.

880
01:11:33.852 --> 01:11:35.187
Pass it here.

881
01:11:35.270 --> 01:11:36.980
-Me too. -Let me do it too.

882
01:11:40.943 --> 01:11:42.069
By the way, No-ma.

883
01:11:42.152 --> 01:11:44.071
Isn't Ga-kyung going to give her fingerprint?

884
01:11:44.154 --> 01:11:45.239
When is she coming back?

885
01:11:46.949 --> 01:11:47.866
Ga-kyung?

886
01:11:50.202 --> 01:11:51.787
I don't think she'll come back.

887
01:11:52.371 --> 01:11:53.539
She won't? Why?

888
01:11:57.251 --> 01:11:58.794
Why would you hit me?

889
01:11:58.877 --> 01:12:01.004
How could you say such awful things to her?

890
01:12:02.464 --> 01:12:03.298
So it's true.

891
01:12:03.382 --> 01:12:06.135
First you serve the Japs like a dog, and now you're messing around with one?

892
01:12:06.218 --> 01:12:07.386
Just like your mom?

893
01:12:10.305 --> 01:12:12.683
A child doesn't get to choose their parents.

894
01:12:12.766 --> 01:12:15.769
That poor thing. Imagine how much she must've struggled

895
01:12:16.812 --> 01:12:18.730
because of her mother, who didn't even raise her.

896
01:12:18.814 --> 01:12:20.107
-No-ma. -It's my fault.

897
01:12:20.190 --> 01:12:22.317
Collect all the petitions for me.

898
01:12:22.401 --> 01:12:23.735
Kkot-nim, I'll be back.

899
01:12:23.819 --> 01:12:24.903
Want another beating?

900
01:12:24.987 --> 01:12:26.738
Bye, No-ma!

901
01:12:32.661 --> 01:12:34.037
You jerks.

902
01:12:35.164 --> 01:12:40.002
I was just getting lucky, and you had to ruin my game, damn it.

903
01:12:46.800 --> 01:12:47.926
My hand!

904
01:12:48.010 --> 01:12:49.595
Get your foot off my hand!

905
01:12:49.678 --> 01:12:52.556
Do you think we're just suckers who burn money on you?

906
01:12:53.140 --> 01:12:56.685
We paid you 50 won to get rid of those filthy shantytown bums.

907
01:12:56.768 --> 01:12:59.438
You should have something to show for it.

908
01:13:02.983 --> 01:13:04.359
Come on, sir.

909
01:13:04.902 --> 01:13:06.737
Fifty won sounds like a lot,

910
01:13:06.820 --> 01:13:09.531
but each household only gets a won or two.

911
01:13:10.032 --> 01:13:13.160
Where are they supposed to go with that?

912
01:13:13.243 --> 01:13:14.244
So,

913
01:13:14.786 --> 01:13:17.247
you blew all that money gambling?

914
01:13:18.123 --> 01:13:20.292
I've done enough.

915
01:13:20.959 --> 01:13:23.212
Then give me another 30 won or so.

916
01:13:24.379 --> 01:13:25.672
Those bums

917
01:13:25.756 --> 01:13:29.510
need a cart to haul their stuff out.

918
01:13:35.599 --> 01:13:37.976
Damn it, you bastards!

919
01:13:47.736 --> 01:13:49.363
Do you think this is a game?

920
01:13:50.280 --> 01:13:51.156
Listen carefully.

921
01:13:53.242 --> 01:13:54.243
Easy with the knife.

922
01:13:54.993 --> 01:13:56.161
You have three days.

923
01:13:56.245 --> 01:13:57.829
Throw them all out by then,

924
01:13:57.913 --> 01:13:59.873
or you'll pay for that 50 won with your life.

925
01:13:59.957 --> 01:14:01.625
How can I do that in three days?

926
01:14:01.708 --> 01:14:03.126
If you can't,

927
01:14:03.210 --> 01:14:05.754
cough up all the money you pocketed.

928
01:14:06.964 --> 01:14:07.798
Is that clear?

929
01:14:07.881 --> 01:14:08.715
Yes, sir.

930
01:14:09.633 --> 01:14:10.884
Crystal clear.

931
01:14:17.766 --> 01:14:18.600
Let's go.

932
01:14:22.437 --> 01:14:24.022
Those rotten thugs.

933
01:14:25.315 --> 01:14:26.817
I almost got myself killed.

934
01:14:28.860 --> 01:14:31.572
How am I supposed to get those bums out?

935
01:14:41.623 --> 01:14:42.457
Right.

936
01:14:43.458 --> 01:14:46.295
Hello, this is the Inspector General's Office.

937
01:14:49.339 --> 01:14:52.217
You must've enjoyed making a fool of me yesterday.

938
01:14:52.926 --> 01:14:55.596
I can't leave my desk for too long.

939
01:14:55.679 --> 01:14:57.306
Please get to the point.

940
01:14:59.099 --> 01:15:00.183
Lee Ga-kyung.

941
01:15:06.440 --> 01:15:08.358
My name is Keum Seo-hee.

942
01:15:09.026 --> 01:15:11.361
I think you've mistaken me for someone else.

943
01:15:11.445 --> 01:15:13.238
In May 1929,

944
01:15:13.989 --> 01:15:15.324
Mount Yebong, Gyeonggi-do.

945
01:15:19.953 --> 01:15:22.497
Shimomura, who lived in Hwanggeumjeong 2-jeongmok,

946
01:15:22.581 --> 01:15:25.834
reportedly got drunk and fell to his death in a valley on Mount Yebong.

947
01:15:26.460 --> 01:15:28.795
The geisha who was there with him,

948
01:15:30.005 --> 01:15:31.632
Sakura, disappeared.

949
01:15:34.301 --> 01:15:37.095
She left nothing but a bloodstained stone on the cliff.

950
01:15:40.432 --> 01:15:44.102
The restaurant owner recognized your photo right away.

951
01:15:47.898 --> 01:15:50.400
Apparently, the 100 won you owed when you were sold

952
01:15:50.901 --> 01:15:53.570
has now grown to 350 won with interest.

953
01:15:54.154 --> 01:15:54.988
Right.

954
01:15:55.781 --> 01:15:56.823
Don't worry.

955
01:15:58.659 --> 01:16:01.578
I didn't tell them you are here.

956
01:16:02.412 --> 01:16:03.246
What is it…

957
01:16:06.708 --> 01:16:08.001
you want to tell me?

958
01:16:09.461 --> 01:16:13.632
Find out who the inspector general meets, what he's up to, and what he's hiding.

959
01:16:14.257 --> 01:16:15.884
Dig up any dirt on him,

960
01:16:15.967 --> 01:16:19.429
anything I can use against him, and report back.

961
01:16:19.513 --> 01:16:20.347
Understood?

962
01:16:21.807 --> 01:16:24.351
How am I supposed to find all that out?

963
01:16:25.102 --> 01:16:26.812
I'm just his secretary.

964
01:16:31.149 --> 01:16:32.234
"Just"?

965
01:16:32.317 --> 01:16:35.153
You're a spy from the Gugukdan, now you're his secretary.

966
01:16:35.237 --> 01:16:36.321
And you call that "just"?

967
01:16:37.364 --> 01:16:40.575
The inspector general could have had you ripped to pieces,

968
01:16:41.702 --> 01:16:44.454
yet instead of arresting you, he made you his secretary.

969
01:16:48.250 --> 01:16:49.334
Why would he do that?

970
01:16:51.420 --> 01:16:54.047
I just can't make sense of this.

971
01:16:55.257 --> 01:16:58.385
I just transferred to where they sent me.

972
01:17:00.220 --> 01:17:01.054
Whatever.

973
01:17:02.514 --> 01:17:07.477
Whether you're with the Gugukdan or not, I couldn't care less right now.

974
01:17:12.107 --> 01:17:14.234
Find dirt on the inspector general.

975
01:17:15.277 --> 01:17:16.778
And whatever you see or hear,

976
01:17:16.862 --> 01:17:19.489
you report to me first, before the inspector general.

977
01:17:20.615 --> 01:17:21.616
If you don't,

978
01:17:22.451 --> 01:17:26.121
you'll be executed for the murder of the mainland Japanese resident.

979
01:17:28.582 --> 01:17:32.544
A Josenjing wench killed a Japanese man and dumped his body?

980
01:17:35.005 --> 01:17:37.841
Imagine how thrilled the Jongno police would be.

981
01:17:41.887 --> 01:17:44.389
Think wisely.

982
01:17:47.434 --> 01:17:48.602
Lee Ga-kyung.

983
01:18:34.064 --> 01:18:35.607
Let me ask you one thing.

984
01:18:35.690 --> 01:18:37.150
Hanako's mom…

985
01:18:39.236 --> 01:18:40.654
Did the Gugukdan kill her?

986
01:18:42.948 --> 01:18:44.115
What do you mean?

987
01:18:44.199 --> 01:18:46.326
That's what the inspector general told me.

988
01:18:47.118 --> 01:18:50.413
She was a spy for the Gugukdan, and when she was no longer useful,

989
01:18:52.290 --> 01:18:53.667
they killed her.

990
01:18:58.088 --> 01:18:58.922
Yes.

991
01:18:59.840 --> 01:19:00.674
That's right.

992
01:19:05.220 --> 01:19:07.347
We were just as responsible for her death.

993
01:19:08.056 --> 01:19:10.267
We tried to save her, but we failed.

994
01:19:12.561 --> 01:19:14.688
Even if I were in the same situation as yesterday,

995
01:19:14.771 --> 01:19:15.981
I'd still save Hanako.

996
01:19:16.064 --> 01:19:16.898
Because to me,

997
01:19:18.525 --> 01:19:20.110
she's not Sato's daughter.

998
01:19:21.653 --> 01:19:24.447
She's the daughter of a woman I sent undercover.

999
01:19:39.629 --> 01:19:41.756
She had another daughter.

1000
01:19:43.300 --> 01:19:45.302
The girl she had before marrying Sato.

1001
01:19:47.596 --> 01:19:49.180
Because of me, that little girl

1002
01:19:49.764 --> 01:19:51.975
was torn away from her mother at a young age

1003
01:19:53.268 --> 01:19:54.811
and ended up dying all alone.

1004
01:19:58.732 --> 01:20:00.317
I'd already let that girl die.

1005
01:20:01.860 --> 01:20:05.196
I couldn't bear to lose Hanako too.

1006
01:20:08.241 --> 01:20:10.619
I don't even know the name of her dead daughter.

1007
01:20:11.703 --> 01:20:14.497
I've carried the guilt over that child for all these years.

1008
01:20:19.377 --> 01:20:20.211
Seo-hee.

1009
01:20:21.755 --> 01:20:22.672
Ga-kyung.

1010
01:20:24.633 --> 01:20:26.259
If anything happens to you…

1011
01:20:29.387 --> 01:20:31.640
I'll carry that pain for the rest of my life.

1012
01:20:45.737 --> 01:20:46.613
I have decided…

1013
01:20:51.493 --> 01:20:53.286
to trust you.

1014
01:20:55.997 --> 01:20:59.542
It doesn't matter if you can't trust me.

1015
01:20:59.626 --> 01:21:01.294
I'm putting my trust in you.

1016
01:21:03.004 --> 01:21:03.922
We have no choice…

1017
01:21:06.216 --> 01:21:09.427
but to trust each other.

1018
01:21:24.025 --> 01:21:24.859
I trust you

1019
01:21:26.486 --> 01:21:27.737
as well.

1020
01:21:54.848 --> 01:21:56.099
Madam.

1021
01:21:59.811 --> 01:22:02.230
I think there's a way…

1022
01:22:13.575 --> 01:22:14.784
to get rid of Sato.

1023
01:22:17.662 --> 01:22:18.496
What?

1024
01:22:19.372 --> 01:22:21.708
You want to do what with me?

1025
01:22:25.003 --> 01:22:26.296
Let's make a deal.

1026
01:23:13.009 --> 01:23:16.930
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

1027
01:23:17.013 --> 01:23:20.517
Sato, Fukuda, and Kim Seung-eok.

1028
01:23:20.600 --> 01:23:23.269
I think these three will go for each other's throats.

1029
01:23:23.353 --> 01:23:25.271
It's like getting bitten by the dog I raised.

1030
01:23:25.355 --> 01:23:27.107
Can you handle it on your own?

1031
01:23:27.190 --> 01:23:28.858
If you bring nothing in three days,

1032
01:23:28.942 --> 01:23:30.610
you'll be in trouble yourself.

1033
01:23:30.693 --> 01:23:32.946
Did you have a good day out today?

1034
01:23:33.029 --> 01:23:34.405
Yes, I had a good time.

1035
01:23:34.489 --> 01:23:35.907
You should be more worried

1036
01:23:35.990 --> 01:23:38.493
about coming back empty-handed than getting caught.

1037
01:23:38.576 --> 01:23:40.662
It has to be the Inspector General's Office cabinet.

1038
01:23:40.745 --> 01:23:42.288
You're still on the Gugukdan's side.

1039
01:23:42.372 --> 01:23:43.957
He's back at the Government-General.

1040
01:23:45.458 --> 01:23:46.960
You think I don't know that?

1041
01:23:52.549 --> 01:23:54.551
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
